+- **Leaving a modal: accidental exits are withdrawn, deliberate ones ask once (#779).** Every modal is a `ModalShell`; `closeOnBackdrop` defaults to **`false`** because a stray click beside the panel is the one exit nobody means to take. A modal with nothing to lose (a read-only viewer, ⌘P, a live-applying picker) passes `closeOnBackdrop` to opt back in — and says why. A form does NOT opt in "only while clean": a stray-click behaviour that depends on what the user has already changed is one they can't predict, and it trains the habit right up to the moment it stops working. (`EntityRecordModal`'s `closeOnBackdrop={!editing}` is not that — it has a genuine read-only mode, and reading is a viewer.) The deliberate exits (Escape, ✕, Cancel) always keep working — ARIA requires Escape, and a modal you can't dismiss is worse than a lost draft — but a modal holding unsaved work wraps its close handler with **`useDirtyClose(dirty, onClose)`** so they ask once first. That is the ONLY way dirtiness is expressed: not a `ModalShell` prop, not a per-modal confirm row. **Every deliberate exit must go through that handler, including the ✕ and Cancel the modal draws itself** — guarding the shell is not guarding the modal, and a ✕ still wired to a bare `onClose` throws the work away in silence while Escape politely asks. Compare with **`sameShape`** (`web/src/lib/sameShape.ts`), never `JSON.stringify`: sparse overrides reshuffle their keys, grant lists reorder, and `JSON.stringify(new Set([...]))` is `{}` for every Set however full — so stringify both invents edits nobody made and misses whole ones. `dirty` is measured against **what the modal opened with**, never "has anything been typed" — a form that seeds a date must not claim unsaved work on sight, and a guard that fires when nothing changed teaches people to click through it. Every modal that guards needs BOTH tests: the dirty case and the clean one. `DialogProvider` sits at the root in `main.tsx` and in `web/src/test/queryWrapper.tsx`, so `useDialog()` resolves the same way under test as in the app. `web/src/components/modalDismissal.test.ts` fails the build on a hand-rolled backdrop.
